{
  "case_id": "regex-word-boundary-empty",
  "claim": "HIR is_match_empty records whether a successful match can have zero length in its surrounding context. Unicode and ASCII word boundaries can match an empty substring in a nonempty haystack; whether they accept an entirely empty haystack is a different question. Corrected positive boundary assertions express this claim; the original negative boundary assertions contradict it. The weak variant is only a removal control and receives no validity or adequacy label.",
  "test_id": "hir::translate::tests::analysis_is_match_empty",
